{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_8","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '1,125p' src/cljc/yang/core/uast.cljc && sed -n '420,485p' src/cljc/yin/vm/integer.cljc && cat deps.edn && sed -n '1,160p' docs/agents/build-n-test.md\"","aggregated_output":"(ns yang.core.uast\n  \"Universal AST constructors shared by every language lowering and prelude. Every\n   function returns a canonical map node (`:literal`, `:variable`, `:lambda`,\n   `:application`, `:if`, `:vm/current-continuation`); nothing here adds a\n   node type.\n\n   `sexp->uast` reads a small s-expression notation into those same nodes so\n   the prelude can be written legibly:\n\n     symbol            -> :variable\n     (fn [params] b)   -> :lambda\n     (if t c a)        -> :if\n     (do a b ... z)    -> sequencing through one-parameter lambdas\n     (let [x v ...] b) -> nested immediately applied lambdas\n     (quote x)         -> :literal x\n     (%capture)        -> :vm/current-continuation\n     (yin/def k v)     -> the definition application\n     (f a ...)         -> :application\n     any other value   -> :literal\"\n  (:require\n    [yang.tails :as tails]\n    [yin.vm :as vm]))\n\n\n(defn lit\n  [x]\n  {:type :literal, :value x})\n\n\n(defn v\n  [sym]\n  {:type :variable, :name sym})\n\n\n(defn lam\n  [params body]\n  {:type :lambda, :params (vec params), :body body})\n\n\n(defn app\n  [op & args]\n  {:type :application, :operator op, :operands (vec args)})\n\n\n(defn if-node\n  [t c a]\n  {:type :if, :test t, :consequent c, :alternate a})\n\n\n(def capture {:type :vm/current-continuation})\n\n\n(defn def!\n  \"`(yin/def key value)`: key is a literal symbol.\"\n  [key value]\n  (app (v 'yin/def) (lit key) value))\n\n\n(def discard\n  \"The parameter a sequencing lambda binds and ignores. `%` cannot begin a\n   Python identifier, so it never shadows a guest name.\"\n  '%_)\n\n\n(defn then\n  \"Evaluate `a` for effect, then `b`.\"\n  [a b]\n  (app (lam [discard] b) a))\n\n\n(defn seq-nodes\n  \"Evaluate every node in order; the value is the last one's.\"\n  [nodes]\n  (reduce (fn [acc node] (then acc node)) (first nodes) (rest nodes)))\n\n\n(defn let1\n  [sym value body]\n  (app (lam [sym] body) value))\n\n\n(defn sexp->uast\n  [form]\n  (cond\n    (symbol? form) (v form)\n    (seq? form)\n    (let [[head & args] form]\n      (case head\n        fn (lam (first args) (sexp->uast (second args)))\n        if (if-node (sexp->uast (first args))\n                    (sexp->uast (second args))\n                    (sexp->uast (nth args 2)))\n        do (seq-nodes (map sexp->uast args))\n        let (let [[bindings body] args]\n              (reduce (fn [inner [sym value]]\n                        (let1 sym (sexp->uast value) inner))\n                      (sexp->uast body)\n                      (reverse (partition 2 bindings))))\n        quote (lit (first args))\n        %capture capture\n        (apply app (sexp->uast head) (map sexp->uast args))))\n    :else (lit form)))\n\n\n(def mark-tails\n  \"`yang.tails/mark-tails`: the lowering marks its tree with the same\n   function a rewriting stage recomputes the marks with.\"\n  tails/mark-tails)\n\n\n;; =============================================================================\n;; Call-site occurrence contract C1 (Addendum A, design §2)\n;; =============================================================================\n;;\n;; Every final `:application` occurrence of a produced tree carries the\n;; reserved frontend-metadata key `:yang/call-site` with version value `1`\n;; as a plain node key. Projection (`yin.vm/ast-side-tables`) drops the key\n;; from canonical rows and emits it into the frontend-metadata side table\n;; as `[origin root-address path :yang/call-site 1]`, where the first\n;; three coordinates are the site id. The key carries no callee identity,\n;; source arity, or ambient classification. It is distinct from\n;; `:yang/site`, the safepoint mark, which travels as node metadata.\n;; Dedicated node kinds (`:dao.stream.apply/call`, stream and\n;; continuation nodes) are not `:application` nodes and are never marked.\n;; The walk lives here, beside the other shared tree transforms, so every\n(defn- int-true-div\n  [_limits a b]\n  (let [x (big! 'true-div 0 a)\n        y (divisor! 'true-div b)]\n    ;; CPython: 0 / -5 is -0.0\n    (ratio->float (magnitude x) (magnitude y)\n                  (not= (neg? (sign x)) (neg? (sign y))))))\n\n\n(defn- float!\n  \"Argument `arg` of `op` as a host double, or a `:wrong-type` refusal.\"\n  [op arg v]\n  (if (host/host-float? v) v (wrong-type! op arg :float)))\n\n\n(defn- int-compare-float\n  [_limits a f]\n  (let [x (big! 'compare-float 0 a)\n        v (float! 'compare-float 1 f)]\n    (cond\n      (host/nan-float? v) (wrong-type! 'compare-float 1 :non-nan-float)\n      (host/infinite-float? v) (if (pos? v) -1 1)\n      :else\n      ;; t = trunc(v): x < t means x < v, x > t means x >= t + 1 > v\n      ;; (or x > t >= v when v is negative); x = t leaves the fraction\n      (let [c (host/compare-big x (float-kernel/trunc-big v))]\n        (cond (not (zero? c)) c\n              (or (>= (float-kernel/signed (neg? v) v) two-53-float)\n                  (= v (host/native->double (host/trunc-native v))))\n              0\n              (pos? v) -1\n              :else 1)))))\n\n\n(defn- int-from-float\n  [limits f]\n  (let [v (float! 'from-float 0 f)]\n    (if (or (host/nan-float? v) (host/infinite-float? v))\n      (wrong-type! 'from-float 0 :finite-float)\n      (out limits (float-kernel/trunc-big v)))))\n\n\n;; =============================================================================\n;; Text\n;; =============================================================================\n\n(def ^:private digit-values\n  \"Each digit character, either letter case, to its value.\"\n  (into {}\n        (mapcat (fn [i]\n                  (let [c (subs \"0123456789abcdefghijklmnopqrstuvwxyz\" i (inc i))]\n                    [[c i] [(str/upper-case c) i]])))\n        (range 36)))\n\n\n(defn- radix!\n  \"Radix argument `r` of `op` as a native integer from 2 to 36.\"\n  [op r]\n  (let [n (big! op 1 r)]\n    (when-not (and (<= 0 (host/compare-big n (host/from-native 2)))\n                   (<= (host/compare-big n (host/from-native 36)) 0))\n      (refuse! op :out-of-range {::arg 1, ::lo 2, ::hi 36}))\n    (host/to-native n)))\n\n\n(defn- power-of-two?\n{:deps {org.clojure/core.async {:mvn/version \"1.8.741\"}\n        org.clojure/tools.reader {:mvn/version \"1.5.0\"}\n        ring/ring {:mvn/version \"1.14.1\"}\n        com.cognitect/transit-clj {:mvn/version \"1.0.333\"}\n        org.replikativ/boring {:mvn/version \"0.1.30\"}\n        com.datomic/peer {:mvn/version \"1.0.7364\"}\n        org.postgresql/postgresql {:mvn/version \"42.7.3\"}\n        org.clojure/data.json {:mvn/version \"2.5.0\"}\n        http-kit/http-kit {:mvn/version \"2.8.0\"}\n        org.jsoup/jsoup {:mvn/version \"1.18.3\"}\n        instaparse/instaparse {:mvn/version \"1.5.0\"}\n        ;; yang.python.antlr: the runtime the generated Python3 parser runs\n        ;; on; pinned to the tool version in :antlr-gen (they are one release)\n        org.antlr/antlr4-runtime {:mvn/version \"4.13.2\"}\n        criterium/criterium {:mvn/version \"0.4.6\"}\n        io.github.rctcwyvrn/blake3 {:mvn/version \"1.3\"}\n        stigmergy/chp {:mvn/version \"0.1.0-SNAPSHOT\"\n                       :exclusions [refactor-nrepl/refactor-nrepl]}}\n :cljd/opts {}\n ;; build/antlr/python3/classes: the generated Python3 parser, produced by\n ;; `clj -M:antlr-gen` (antlr/python3/manifest.edn); absent until generated\n :paths [\"src/clj\" \"src/cljc\" \"src/cljs\" \"src/cljd\"\n         \"build/antlr/python3/classes\" \"build/antlr/php/classes\"\n         \"build/antlr/typescript/classes\"]\n :aliases {:clean {:extra-paths [\"src/dev\"]\n                   :exec-fn clean/clean}\n           :profile-btree {:extra-paths [\"src/dev\"]\n                           :extra-deps {persistent-sorted-set/persistent-sorted-set\n                                        {:mvn/version \"0.3.0\"}}\n                           :main-opts [\"-m\" \"btree-bench\"]}\n           :test {:extra-paths [\"test\"]\n                  :extra-deps {io.github.cognitect-labs/test-runner\n                               {:git/tag \"v0.5.1\" :git/sha \"dfb30dd\"}\n                               ;; latte-kernel: the LaTTe proof assistant's kernel,\n                               ;; the differential oracle for the yang.clojure gap\n                               ;; program (pinned; MIT; dependency-free)\n                               latte-kernel/latte-kernel\n                               {:git/url \"https://github.com/latte-central/latte-kernel\"\n                                :git/sha \"86fca0d1d054af005cb37395eae04500d45e6279\"}}\n                  ;; The guest recursion limit allows depth that needs more than the\n                  ;; JVM's platform default thread stack (1024 KB on Linux, 2048 KB on\n                  ;; macOS): under 1 MB the guard loses to a JVM StackOverflowError\n                  ;; before it can raise Python's RecursionError, so the same tests\n                  ;; pass on macOS and fail on Linux. 4 MB is twice the measured\n                  ;; macOS-default minimum, leaving headroom as the prelude grows.\n                  ;; Evidence: docs/agents/known-gaps.md (the recursion rows).\n                  ;; merged stack policy: -Xss64m supersedes the earlier -Xss4m —\n                  ;; deep assertion payloads (the PHPT selection diagnostics and\n                  ;; the conformance compositions) overflow smaller stacks in\n                  ;; clojure.test's printer on shiva (verified green at -Xss64m;\n                  ;; the 4m minimum for the prelude recursion rows still holds)\n                  :jvm-opts [\"-Xss64m\"]\n                  :main-opts [\"-m\" \"cognitect.test-runner\"]\n                  :exec-fn cognitect.test-runner.api/test}\n           :nREPL {:extra-paths [\"test\"]\n                   :extra-deps {nrepl/nrepl {:mvn/version \"1.0.0\"}\n                                cider/cider-nrepl {:mvn/version \"0.58.0\"}}\n                   :main-opts [\"-m\" \"nrepl.cmdline\" \"--middleware\" \"[cider.nrepl/cider-middleware]\"]}\n           :cljs {:extra-paths [\"test\" \"src/dev\" \"build/antlr/python3/js\" \"build/antlr/php/js\"]\n                  :extra-deps {thheller/shadow-cljs {:mvn/version \"3.3.5\"}\n                               reagent/reagent {:mvn/version \"2.0.1\"}\n                               com.cognitect/transit-cljs {:mvn/version \"0.8.280\"}}}\n           :dev {:extra-paths [\"src/dev\"]\n                 :extra-deps {thheller/shadow-cljs {:mvn/version \"3.3.5\"}\n                              cider/cider-nrepl {:mvn/version \"0.58.0\"}\n                              reagent/reagent {:mvn/version \"2.0.1\"}\n                              com.cognitect/transit-cljs {:mvn/version \"0.8.280\"}\n                              ;; benchmark baseline + psset-fixtures\n                              ;; generator only; production uses\n                              ;; dao.data.btree\n                              persistent-sorted-set/persistent-sorted-set\n                              {:mvn/version \"0.3.0\"}}\n                 :jvm-opts [\"-Dconfig=config.clj\"]}\n           ;; The one ClojureDart pin. Compose it with the build aliases:\n           ;; clj -M:clojuredart:cljd ..., clj -M:clojuredart:cljd-yin-repl-build ...\n           :clojuredart {:extra-deps {sonwh98/clojuredart\n                                      {:git/url \"https://github.com/sonwh98/ClojureDart.git\"\n                                       :sha \"7d00ee2aa7fa9d990581e78ebc4a66b93cb70a31\"}\n                                      }}\n           :cljd {:extra-paths [\"test\"]\n                  :main-opts [\"-m\" \"cljd.build\"]\n                  :cljd/opts {:kind :flutter :main datomworld.demo.main}}\n           :server {:extra-deps {http-kit/http-kit {:mvn/version \"2.8.0\"}}\n                    :jvm-opts [\"-Dconfig=config.clj\"]\n                    :main-opts [\"-m\" \"world.server\"]}\n           :clj-yin-repl {:main-opts [\"-m\" \"yin.shell.main\"]}\n           ;; jolt host configuration (docs/design/yin.repl-jolt-implementation.md\n           ;; §4.2-4.3), run through build/tools/jolt/bin/jolt -Srepro -M:jolt.\n           ;; src/jolt precedes src/cljc so a host override wins; src/clj is\n           ;; listed for audited portable namespaces only (its JVM namespaces\n           ;; are selected away by :jolt reader branches, never loaded). No\n           ;; generated Java parser classes, no JS/Dart roots, and no\n           ;; dependency coordinate is fetched until a jolt-loaded namespace\n           ;; needs one.\n           :jolt {:replace-paths [\"src/jolt\" \"src/cljc\" \"src/clj\"]\n                  :replace-deps {}}\n           :jolt-yin-repl {:main-opts [\"-m\" \"yin.shell.main\"]}\n           ;; composed after :jolt (-M:jolt:jolt-test): the oracle tests and\n           ;; src/dev (src/dev/jolt_test_runner.clj and its sentinel)\n           :jolt-test {:extra-paths [\"test\" \"src/dev\"]}\n           ;; DIAGNOSTIC only (-M:jolt:jolt-diag:jolt-test): a jolt stand-in\n           ;; for the corpus loader dao.jing.cbor-fixtures, whose root must\n           ;; precede test (src/dev/jolt_diag/dao/jing/cbor_fixtures.cljc);\n           ;; jolt puts :extra-paths roots first, in alias order (-Spath)\n           :jolt-diag {:extra-paths [\"src/dev/jolt_diag\"]}\n           :cljs-yin-repl\n           {:extra-paths [\"test\" \"src/dev\"]\n            :extra-deps {thheller/shadow-cljs {:mvn/version \"3.3.5\"}\n                         reagent/reagent {:mvn/version \"2.0.1\"}\n                         com.cognitect/transit-cljs {:mvn/version \"0.8.280\"}}\n            :main-opts [\"-m\" \"yin.repl.node-runner\"]}\n           :fmt {:extra-paths [\"src/dev\"]\n                 :exec-fn tasks/fix-all}\n           ;; Build-time generation of the grammars-v4 Python3 parser.\n           ;; The tool version must equal the antlr4-runtime above.\n           :antlr-gen {:extra-paths [\"src/dev\"]\n                       :extra-deps {org.antlr/antlr4 {:mvn/version \"4.13.2\"}}\n                       :main-opts [\"-m\" \"yang-antlr-gen\"]}\n           :kondo {:extra-deps {clj-kondo/clj-kondo {:mvn/version \"2026.01.19\"}}\n                   :main-opts [\"-m\" \"clj-kondo.main\"]}\n           ;; Development/oracle only (datomic-q-v1 Client oracle runner,\n           ;; docs/design/dao.space.query.datomic-compat.md); never a production\n           ;; dependency. Backend deps/config are pinned separately once selected.\n           :oracle {:extra-paths [\"src/dev\" \"test\"]\n                    :extra-deps {com.datomic/client-api {:mvn/version \"1.0.69\"}\n                                 ;; oracle backend: Datomic Local, in-process,\n                                 ;; run in docker/oracle (dev-scope only)\n                                 com.datomic/local {:mvn/version \"1.0.301\"}}}\n           :dbg {:extra-paths [\"test\"]\n                 :main-opts [\"-m\" \"debug-cljd\"]\n                 :cljd/opts {:kind :flutter :main datomworld.demo.main}}\n           :cljd-yin-repl {:main-opts [\"-m\" \"yin.repl.runner\"]}\n           :cljd-yin-repl-build\n           {:main-opts  [\"-m\" \"cljd.build\"]\n            :cljd/opts  {:kind       :dart\n                         :main       yin.shell.main\n                         :output-dir \"build/yin-repl\"\n                         :output-to  \"build/yin-repl/yin_repl.dart\"}}\n           :dep-graph {:extra-paths [\"src/dev\"]\n                       :extra-deps {org.clojure/tools.namespace {:mvn/version \"1.5.0\"}}\n                       :main-opts [\"-m\" \"dep-graph\"]}}}\n\n\n;; clj -X:fmt\n\n;; clj -M:nREPL\n\n;; clj -M:nREPL:server\n;; clj -M:test\n;; clj -M:test -n yin.vm-literal-test\n;; clj -M:test -n yin.vm-continuation-test\n;; clj -M:test -n yin.repl.python-antlr-test\n;; clj -X:test :nses '[yin.vm-literal-test yin.vm-test]'\n;; clj -M:test -v yin.vm-addition-test/test-lambda-with-multiple-operations\n\n;; clj -X:clean\n\n;; npx shadow-cljs compile test && node target/node-tests.js\n;; npx shadow-cljs release demo\n;; clj -M:dev -m shadow.cljs.devtools.cli watch demo\n;; clj -M:cljs -m shadow.cljs.devtools.cli watch demo\n;; clj -M:cljs -m shadow.cljs.devtools.cli compile demo\n;; clj -M:cljs -m shadow.cljs.devtools.cli release demo\n\n\n;; mise exec -- clj -M:clojuredart:cljd watch \n;; mise exec -- flutter run \n\n;; To start the emulator:                                                                                              ;; emulator -avd Pixel_3_API_34\n;; flutter emulators --launch Pixel_3_API_34\n;; emulator -avd Pixel_3_API_34 -no-snapshot-load  \n;; emulator -list-avds\n\n;;  clj -M:dep-graph                    # full report + dep-graph.dot + dep-graph.svg\n;;  clj -M:dep-graph --filter \"yin.*\"   # only yin namespaces\n;;  clj -M:dep-graph --layout circo     # choose graphviz layout engine\n---\ndescription: Build, lint, test commands, TDD guidelines, and bracket debugging for Clojure, ClojureScript, Node.js, and ClojureDart\n---\n\n# BUILD & TEST\n\n## Commands\n\n```sh\n# Tests (Babashka runner)\nbb test              # All three lanes (JVM, Node, Dart), fast default form: no slow tests\nbb test:all          # Every test on every lane, slow ones included (JVM takes 20+ min)\nbb test:slow         # Only the slow tests, on every lane\n# One lane alone: <task>:clj, <task>:cljs, <task>:cljd\nbb test:clj          # JVM, fast: skips ^:slow (bare `clj -M:test` runs them too)\nbb test:cljs         # Node (shadow-cljs :cljs alias), fast: guarded slow bodies print SKIP\nbb test:cljd         # Dart (needs flutter on PATH), fast: guarded slow bodies print SKIP\nbb test:all:clj      # JVM, no filter: `clojure -M:test`\nbb test:all:cljs     # Node with DATOM_SLOW_TESTS=1\nbb test:all:cljd     # Dart with DATOM_SLOW_TESTS=1\nbb test:slow:clj     # JVM: `-i :slow` (long-loops-test, ~14 min)\nbb test:slow:cljs    # Node: only the namespaces that use dao.test-slow/guard, DATOM_SLOW_TESTS=1\nbb test:slow:cljd    # Dart: only those namespaces' generated tests, DATOM_SLOW_TESTS=1\n# Slow tests: tag a deftest ^:slow. The JVM runner then excludes it from `bb test:clj`.\n# Node and Dart have no tag filter, so a .cljc slow test also wraps its body in\n# (dao.test-slow/guard \"name\" (fn [] ...)); it prints SKIP unless DATOM_SLOW_TESTS=1.\n# Node and Dart select slow tests by NAMESPACE (derived by grepping `slow/guard`\n# under test/), so the non-slow tests inside those namespaces also run there.\n# On Node, shadow also runs the test namespaces those nine require (about\n# seven more, e.g. lower-portable-test); on Dart only the nine namespaces run.\n# Run test:slow / test:all before a big merge or a commit that touches many parts.\n# Run one Dart lane at a time per machine (the limit is cores and the Flutter cache,\n# not subsystems). On the many-core remote hosts see \"Remote test servers\" below for\n# which lanes may overlap.\n#\n# When to tag a test slow: when it takes more than about 5 s on any lane (the\n# Python e2e tests sit on a ~3 s floor, so their JVM cut is 3.0 s). The\n# default lanes must stay in minutes; 22 JVM tests (0.75% of the suite) were\n# 81% of its test time. Tag it ^:slow on the JVM; if it is a .cljc test, also\n# wrap its body in dao.test-slow/guard so Node and Dart skip it by default. A\n# test that is slow only on Dart (dao.jing.dht-test/unproven-chunks-... takes\n# 72 s there, 3.6 s on the JVM) is a candidate for a speed investigation first.\n# Python slow set (2026-10-06): 65 ^:slow and 15 guard-only tests in the\n# yang.python.antlr e2e, e2e-c1, prelude-parity, safepoint, float-address\n# and int-contract tests; a Python slice landing runs `bb test:sub:clj yang.python --slow`\n# (or `clojure -M:test -i :slow -n <ns>`).\n# While iterating, use the Gate Ladder (see below): G0 iterate via `bb test:sub:clj <own>`\n# or `clojure -M:test -n <ns>`. Do not run the full `bb test` while iterating.\n# When a test fails, reproduce and fix it by running ONLY the failing test\n# (`clojure -M:test -n <ns> -v <ns>/<var>`, Node `--test=<ns>`, Dart `--only <ns>`) --\n# never the whole suite (owner ruling 2026-11-01; see Gate Ladder G0).\n# Individual tests run fine on the laptop; suite-scale runs (G1 subsystem sets,\n# G2 changed sets, full suites, slow tier, nightly) run on shiva/jupiter --\n# the suite has outgrown the laptop (owner ruling 2026-11-04).\n# At slice checkpoints, run G1 (`bb test:sub <own>`). Before landing a slice, run\n# G2 (`bb test:changed` in the worktree across all three lanes).\n# Full repo-wide `bb test` runs once daily on the remote hosts (04:00 VN);\n# a MERGE needs only the affected tests (bb test:changed) -- owner ruling 2026-11-01;\n# for a fix branch, the previously-failing tests green IS the merge bar\n# (owner ruling 2026-11-07; see Gate Ladder G0).\n# Cross-host bugs show only on Node or Dart, so tri-host verification is mandatory\n# for every gate from G1 upward. Run one lane set at a time per machine to avoid\n# contention (a laptop has 8 cores; the 24- and 48-core remote hosts have room to\n# overlap lanes, see \"Remote test servers\" below).\n# Measured fast-lane times (2026-10-03): bb test about 14 min = JVM 5.5 + Node\n# 3.8 + Dart 4.3, plus builds. test:slow: Node and Dart about 5 min each (mostly\n# compile); the JVM half is estimated at 17 min (long-loops-test alone is 14),\n# not yet run end to end. test:all: JVM 20+ min, also an estimate.\nnpm test             # Node.js tests\n\n# Cross-host peers the JVM lane spawns. `bb test` builds both. A bare\n# `bb test:clj` builds only the Node REPL (it depends on build:yin-repl-node);\n# without build:yin-repl-peer first, the Dart-peer tests skip with a printed notice.\n# Under `bb test:sub` and `bb test:changed`, prerequisites are derived automatically.\nbb build:yin-repl-peer   # Dart exe build/yin-repl-peer (yin.repl R5 pairs)\nbb build:yin-repl-node   # Node REPL target/yin-repl.js; REQUIRED by\n                         # yin.repl.dht-process-test (JVM-to-Node DHT reader,\n                         # and the linker L5 Node reader that requires a module\n                         # by name): `clojure -M:test` without it fails that test\n```\n\n### Changed-only tests: `bb test:changed`\n\n`bb test:changed` (src/dev/affected.clj) runs the fast tests a change can\nreach: the reverse require closure of the files changed since the\nmerge-base with master, plus fixtures that mention a changed resource path,\ntests that walk a changed tree, and each src file's `_test` by convention.\nA walker is a file calling file-seq, fs/glob, fs/list-dir,\nfs/walk-file-tree or .listFiles; each string literal argument of its\nio/file, fs/file, fs/path, fs/glob, java.io.File. or File. calls is a root\n(let-bound roots count), and a change under a root selects it. The three\nlanes run in parallel (logs: target/profile/changed-<lane>.log) after the\nneeded builds. `test:changed:list` shows what and why; `:clj`/`:cljs`/\n`:cljd` run one lane; `--base REF`; `--changed FILE...` (absolute OK; a\ntypo, an empty list or the wrong cwd exits 1). Use it to iterate and to\nland a slice confined to a package. Exit 2 (from :list too) is a wide\nchange (deps.edn bb.edn shadow-cljs.edn mise.toml .cljstyle src/dev/\nantlr/ .clj-kondo/ package*/pubspec*): it runs nothing; run `bb test`,\nas for a change to the core everything requires (yin.vm engine,\ndao.stream, codecs) and before a big merge. Not seen: dynamic loads\n(`requiring-resolve`, `resolve`), paths or walk roots built at run time,\nand spawned programs that changed (target/yin-repl.js, Dart peers).\n\n### Sharded quick JVM feedback and change routing\n\n```sh\nbb test:quick-sharded                           # Full G3-sized JVM quick lane, 4 workers\nbb test:quick-sharded --changed src/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc\nbb test:quick-sharded --base master --workers 6  # Changed selection, explicit worker limit\nbb test:quick-sharded --list --changed src/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc\nbb test:routed docs/agents/build-n-test.md       # Explicit changed paths (absolute OK)\nbb test:routed --dry-run deps.edn               # Print dispatch; executes no gate\nbb test:routed                                 # Git change set, same base as test:changed\nbb deps:npm                                    # Content-checked local npm ci\nbb -cp src/dev -m quick-sharded-test            # Runner/routing/cache self-tests\n```\n\n`test:quick-sharded` is a JVM-only execution alternative for broad G2 and\nthe JVM portion of G3. Without selection flags it selects every JVM test;\n`--changed FILE...` or `--base REF` uses `affected/select` and\n`affected/lane-tests`, exactly as `test:changed:clj` does. Wide input selects\nthe full JVM set here. It never changes `test:changed`'s selection or exit-2\nsemantics. `--workers N` must be positive (default 4 on the laptop).\n\nShard membership comes from every entry in `src/dev/subsystems.edn`, using\n`affected/select-subsystems` and the same longest-prefix ownership rule as\n`test:sub`. As in the shiva script below, currently unowned namespaces run\nin an explicit `unmapped` residual shard, printed by name. Registry omissions\ntherefore cannot silently shrink coverage. Each nonempty shard gets its own\n`clojure -M:test -e :slow -n <ns> ...` process, with at most N JVMs running.\nPrerequisites are derived from the entire selected JVM reach and finish\nserially before workers start; the Node REPL build prerequisite\n(`build:yin-repl-node`) also ensures `bb deps:npm`.\n\nEach invocation writes a separate `target/profile/quick-sharded-<id>/`:\n`selected.txt`, `ns-<shard>.txt`, `covered.txt`, `uncovered.txt`, per-shard logs,\nand `summary.edn`. Before execution it checks **set equality** between selected\nnamespaces and the union of shard lists, plus absence of duplicate assignments.\nAny uncovered, unexpected, or duplicate namespace fails loudly before tests.\nThe final summary totals tests, assertions, failures and errors and separates\nJVM wall time from total time including selection/builds. A nonzero child exit,\nfailure/error, or missing final test-runner summary makes the task exit nonzero.\nDry plans write namespace evidence but execute no builds or tests. An empty\nselection prints `0 JVM namespaces selected` and exits 1, including dry plans.\nThe final `summary.edn` includes a `:verification-scope` record; the same EDN\nrecord is printed on stdout with `:type :verification-scope`, `:runner`,\n`:scope`, `:exit`, `:dry-run?`, and `:gate-complete?`. JVM feedback always has\n`:scope :jvm-feedback` and `:gate-complete? false`, even on exit 0.\n\n`test:routed <changed-files...>` applies this priority table to the whole change\nset, prints the exact dispatch, executes it and propagates its result:\n\n+----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+-----------------------------------------------------------------------+\n| Change class (first match wins)                                                              | Dispatch                                                              |\n+==============================================================================================+=======================================================================+\n| Existing wide inputs (`deps.edn`, `bb.edn`, `src/dev/`, ANTLR, package locks, runner         | `bb test` — full quick tri-host; success required                     |\n| configs, etc.), toolchain manifests, CI workflows, build scripts                             |                                                                       |\n+----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+-----------------------------------------------------------------------+\n| Only `.md`, `.txt`, `.rst` documentation, excluding test resources                           | `git diff --check HEAD -- <paths>` — documentation whitespace/format  |\n|                                                                                              | lint only                                                             |\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
