{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_9","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"rg -n '\"'^### 5.2|''^### 7.2|''^## 9|P0′|C4|C5|collision|compare-float|boxed'\"' docs/design/yang.preludes.md && sed -n '375,465p' docs/design/yang.preludes.md && sed -n '740,850p' docs/design/yang.preludes.md\"","aggregated_output":"14:- **2026-11-21 (r5 → r6 hybrid architecture & focused profile scope):** Eliminated guest-UAST host-leak workarounds and collapsed fragmented control subsystems into a **three-tier hybrid model** (aligned with Unison, Koka, and OCaml 5): (1) promoted representation-sensitive pure ops (`data/float64?`, `data/equiv`, `data/canonical-compare`, `data/canonical-entries`, `data/admit-key?`, `kind/namespace`, and boxed IEEE-754 `yin.vm.float`) into `:pure` host primitives backed by `dao.jing.cbor` / `dao.host.*`, eliminating raw-double stack-frame hazards and guest-side $O(n \\log n)$ sorting; (2) unified `yrt.escape`, `yrt.gen`, safepoint interrupt dispatch, and cold error/limit policy traps into one composable guest algebraic-effect layer (`yrt.effect`) over `%capture` with zero Jolt kernel expansion; (3) focused swappable preludes on **Native profiles** (`py`, `js`, `php`, `clj` for existing code in those languages) plus **N → 1 Yin/Clojure profiles** (`yang.python/clojure-core-v1`, future `yang.typescript/clojure-core-v1`), dropping unnecessary off-diagonal N×M symmetry (such as `:yang.clojure/py-v1`).\n15:- **2026-11-21 (r7 → r8 reconciliation):** Addressed all findings from the r7 architect review (thread `01a1faa3-bb7e-7c30-b3bf-cedbad008bfc`; 8 HIGH, 1 MEDIUM, plus default-profile regressions): (H1) explicit default-selector mechanism — the composition's immutable configuration carries the preferred `[id revision]`, applied at the normal request entry, with two-revision / legacy-pin / in-flight-snapshot gates; (H2) per-frontend **entry-lowering contracts** emitting the landed native entry shapes (`py` 1-arg `run-main`, `js` 1-operand, `php` 2-or-4 with request stream) alongside the Clojure resolver-bearing 2-arg shape; (H3) ONE derivation record (frontend/lowerer revision, descriptor, resolved runtime closure, input, output), pins reconciled by module symbol before lowering, dependency-first installation in linked composition, resolver derivation in provenance / live cell in the task; (H4) complete effect-unwind traversal per frame kind with exactly-once cleanup, a P2′ cold-error policy for plain `yang.clojure`, `clojure.core.impl` owning zero cells while declaring its runtime effects; (H5) address-bound export-**role** evidence (same-arity wrong-role fails closed); (H6) the §5.1 example labeled a Track B recipe recording bundled shape, linked trailing forms, pins, and C1 behavior independently; (H7) slice repair — P1′ clj-only synthetic fixtures, P2′ native collection invocation + bundled shadowing, P3′ the real cross-syntax unwind; (H8) boxed conversion/true-division at the host boundary, zero-raw-double scoped to boxed-path profiles; (M9) `yang.core.defquoted` naming consistency, r6 gates attached verbatim to Track B, oracle assignment (legacy pins ← native oracles, default ← capability refusals); (R) default-profile regressions — unqualified `:k` admission, cross-carrier integer identity, `:clj/unbound` distinguishability, canonical order settled to Jing encoded-byte order.\n16:- **2026-11-21 (r6 → r7 Clojure-First Default & Legacy Track, plus landed-DRY reconciliation):** Three owner directives. **(D10) Default-profile inversion:** for `yang.python` (and later `yang.typescript`/`yang.php`), the **N → 1 Yin/Clojure profile is the DEFAULT** runtime profile; the native preludes (`py`/`js`/`php` semantics) become the **Legacy compatibility track** — kept frozen as landed (they already exist, oracle-parity-proven, at their current content addresses), with their *re-architecture* onto `yrt.*`/boxed float deferred until legacy demand justifies it. **(Clojure-first roadmap):** the implementation order re-sequenced so the Clojure prelude family (`yrt.effect`/`yrt.int` with Clojure-only consumers, unified trusted `clj`, `clojure.core.impl` + `clojure.core` facade, `clj.py`, the python lowerer's descriptor parameterization) is built FIRST — the other-language native preludes are untouched by those slices (zero golden churn; defquoted consolidation and emitter standardization for py/ts/php defer to the legacy track). **(DRY-alignment reconciliation):** §5.2 admission checks home in `yang.core.prelude-admission` (3→5 publics, at bound) keeping `yang.core.prelude` pure emission; §8.2 names both the guest linker modules (`yrt.*`) and their host emitter namespaces (`src/cljc/yang/rt/*.cljc`) and acknowledges the analyzer's 3 self-loop warnings (macro self-reference, no multi-node cycles); defquoted consolidation accounted against the public-surface ledger; §2 gains the tao-architecture second-axiom alignment (the semantics descriptor is stream-resident interpreter configuration; the provenance tuple names the interpreter).\n91:3. **No raw callbacks & no raw host doubles in guest frames:** Policy handlers and closures passed into `yrt.*` are ordinary guest Yin closures, never host-boundary callbacks. By boxing IEEE-754 float operations at the `yin.vm.float` host boundary, unwrapped host doubles never appear on guest stacks **on boxed-path profiles (the Clojure family)**, making `%capture` and safepoints safe there — the frozen native preludes retain their landed, separately-validated numerics until Track B (r8 scope note).\n138:| **Tier 1: Native Host `:pure` Core** | Host module exports (`:pure`, effects `#{}`) in `data`, `integer`, `float`, `kind` | **All four hold:** (1) one universal mathematical/representational truth across all languages and all 4 hosts; (2) host-representation-sensitive (avoids `Float64`/`BigInt`/keyword/HAMT leaks); (3) total or status-returning without suspending control flow or calling guest closures; (4) hot-path value operation. | Exact big-int math, boxed IEEE-754 float math & formatting, `data/float64?`, `data/equiv`, `data/canonical-compare`, `data/canonical-entries`, `data/admit-key?`, `kind/namespace`, code-point strings. |\n171:   - **`data/admit-key? [k]`:** Recursive portable key/element predicate preventing host map/set collapse (`yin/vm/data.cljc:34–36`, `dao.jing.cbor.md:173, 266`). Returns `true` iff `k` (recursively across vectors, maps, and sets) contains only `nil`, booleans, exact integers, strings, and keywords/symbols whose `name` is free of `\"/\"` and not starting with `\":\"` — **an absent namespace is admitted (r8): the namespace-non-empty rule applies to two-part keywords only, so an unqualified `:k` admits**. Returns `false` for any `float64?` (at any nesting depth), ambiguous identifiers, seqs/lists, closures/continuations, or `:cell-ref` handles. **Integer-carrier normalization (r8):** distinct exact-integer carriers (`int64` vs boxed) normalize recursively on insertion AND lookup so equal integers hit the same entry.\n174:2. **Boxed IEEE-754 host module `yin.vm.float` (`src/cljc/yin/vm/float.cljc`, module name `'float`):** **Host-boundary conversion rule (r8):** boxed conversion and true-division results are exposed AT the host boundary (`integer/to-float` results and `true-div` quotients enter guest frames only as boxed `data/float64`); the zero-raw-double guarantee is scoped to profiles on the boxed path (the Clojure-family profiles). The frozen native ABI of the legacy preludes is unchanged.\n175:   - Operates exclusively on **boxed `data/float64`** inputs and outputs (plus exact integers where specified), returning either a boxed `data/float64`, a boolean/integer/string, or a pure status keyword (`:yin.vm.float/div-zero`, `:yin.vm.float/underflow`, `:yin.vm.float/out-of-range`, `:yin.vm.float/fractional-exp`, `:yin.vm.float/infinite-exp`).\n179:     - Core IEEE arithmetic: `add`, `sub`, `mul`, `div` (returns boxed IEEE result, or `:yin.vm.float/div-zero` on `div-checked` when `y == 0.0`), `neg` (preserves `-0.0 ↔ +0.0`), `abs`, `compare` (`-1`/`0`/`1` or `:yin.vm.float/nan`).\n180:     - Division/floor/power: `floor` (total IEEE double floor), `floor-int` (exact integer for finite `|x| < 2^53`, else `:yin.vm.float/out-of-range`), `fmod-pos` (Sterbenz remainder for finite `x >= 0, y > 0`), `floordiv-mod` (returns `[q r]` boxed pair or `:yin.vm.float/div-zero`, preserving `-0.0` quotient sign and `2.1 // 0.7 == 3.0` rounding correction), `fpow-half` (half-power squaring for `py`/`js`/`clj.py`), `fpow-base` (base squaring for `php`, preserving `1.1 ** 6` bit-exact oracle parity — see D7), `neg-pow` (`[x n pow-order]`, returns boxed `float64` or `:yin.vm.float/underflow`), `parts` (`[mantissa exp2]` exact integer pair).\n254:1. **`:yang.prelude/recipe` (host-side compiler recipe that *emits* a runtime module) — the example below is a TRACK B recipe** (a legacy re-architecture recipe for a native prelude; the P0′ recipes for the Clojure-family modules use the standardized fields):\n301:### 5.2 Composition rules and verified-closure admission\n306:2. **Export collision rule (qualified vs. projected):** Distinct Layer-2a/2b/2c modules may share bare local export names across qualified module borders; collisions are refused on duplicate linker module symbols, duplicate stripped local `module-definitions` keys, or duplicate source-facing `:ambient-projections` aliases (`§6.3`).\n310:6. **Dual-emitter standardization & Parity Law:** Standardized linked emission applies to the **P0′ Clojure-family modules** (`:trailing-requires []`, `:finalize-c1? true`) — it does NOT retroactively standardize the frozen native preludes (r8: landed `py` ends its module tree with `require yang.call` and has no C1 finalizer there; php likewise; the bundled clojure continuation family is a left fold — the `:mode` field alone cannot freeze these, so each frozen runtime records its bundled shape, linked trailing forms, dependency pins, and C1 side-table identity-or-absence **independently**). Any program compiled under a composed prelude MUST produce identical outcomes in bundled and linked modes across the semantic, stack, and register VMs (and the AST walker once L-b lands).\n321:2. **Native language profiles (`py`, `js`, `php` — the Legacy compatibility track, built later):** Preserve full, faithful CPython/Node/PHP semantics for existing libraries and code that assumes them. The landed preludes already provide this at their current content addresses and remain the regression net (their oracle suites keep passing untouched). What defers is their *re-architecture* onto `yrt.*`/boxed float — a separate legacy-modernization track, undertaken only when legacy demand justifies it. Until then they run exactly as landed: frozen mechanisms, zero golden churn, selectable by pinning their revision.\n514:### 7.2 Portable numeric & collection contract (`clj.py` over `:pure` host core + `yrt.effect`)\n525:2. **Int × Int:** Delegates directly to `yin.vm.integer` (`add`, `sub`, `neg`, `mul`, `floor-div-mod`, `pow`, `true-div`, `compare`), checking `b == 0` beforehand (performing `:math/div-zero`) and passing every result through `yrt.int/check-limit` before indexing `[q r]` pairs or chaining into further ops. **All host-boundary float carriers are boxed (r8):** `integer/to-float-boxed` for promotion, `integer/true-div-boxed` for division quotients, and boxed `float/neg-pow` for negative exponents — no raw host double enters a guest frame on any Clojure-family numeric path. The frozen native ABI (`integer/to-float`, `true-div`) is unchanged for the legacy track. **Boxed comparison (r8, VM-engineer review):** `integer/compare-float-boxed [x-boxed y-boxed]` (and `integer/from-float-boxed`) are added to the integer host-module exports (listed in §7.2's boxed-path usage) — the landed `compare-float`/`from-float` take raw host doubles and are legacy-only; mixed int×float comparisons on the boxed path never unwrap.\n527:   - Exact ints promote via `(data/float64 (yrt.int/check-limit (clj/rt-ctx) (integer/to-float-boxed i)))` — `integer/to-float-boxed` (r8) returns the boxed carrier at the host boundary so no raw host double crosses a guest frame.\n528:   - `+`, `-`, `*`, unary `-`, unary `+`, `/`, `//`, `%`, `**`, and `<`/`<=`/`>`/`>=` delegate directly to boxed `yin.vm.float` exports (`float/add`, `float/sub`, `float/mul`, `float/neg`, `float/div-checked`, `float/floordiv-mod`, `float/fpow-half`, `float/neg-pow`, `float/compare`) and `integer/compare-float` (via boxed float helper).\n559:- `clj` exports collision-free primitive helpers **`clj/prim-get`** and **`clj/prim-assoc`**. **Bundled-mode door enforcement (r8, VM-engineer review):** in bundled mode the door effects are honored ONLY for the emitted `clj` definition addresses — the VM admits a provenance-door call by the calling definition's recorded address, never by name resolution from guest scope, so a forged co-bundled call cannot mint provenance (linked mode already gates by content address/admission).\n571:In Slice P3, the portable Clojure standard library splits into two Layer-2c linker modules — eliminating store-key collisions against VM primitives while publishing cell-free 0-arg export accessors:\n575:   - **Zero bare primitive store collisions:** Every definition is prefixed `impl-*` (`impl-identity`, `impl-get`, `impl-assoc`, `impl-conj`, etc.), so internal calls to `(get m k)`, `(assoc m k v)`, `(conj xs x)`, `(first xs)`, `(rest xs)`, `(vec xs)`, `(nil? x)`, `(empty? xs)`, `(not b)` resolve directly to VM primitives.\n612:- **Zero bare integral float literals & zero raw host doubles in guest UAST:** All float operations pass boxed `data/float64` through `yin.vm.float`, avoiding raw host doubles across JVM, Node, Dart, and Jolt.\n640:## 9. Phased implementation roadmap and acceptance gates\n642:**r7 reordering (owner directive D10 — Clojure-first):** the Clojure prelude family is built FIRST; the native py/js/php preludes are untouched by these slices (frozen as landed, zero golden churn), with their `yrt.*`/boxed-float re-architecture deferred to the legacy track (Track B). The original r6 P1–P4 order is superseded; its non-Clojure legs reappear in Track B.\n646:| **P0′ — Composition plumbing & `:pure` host core extensions** | Implement `:yang.prelude/recipe` / `:yang.prelude/profile`, `validate-profile` + `admit-profile` **in `yang.core.prelude-admission`** (3→5 publics, per the §5.2 home rule); add `:pure` host exports (`data/float64?`, `data/equiv`, `data/admit-key?`, `data/canonical-compare`, `data/canonical-entries`, `kind/namespace`, and boxed `yin.vm.float` across all 4 hosts); consolidate `defquoted` into `yang.core.defquoted` (dedicated host macro namespace, keeping `yang.core.prelude` at 11 publics — naming per r8 M9, consistent across §8.1/§8.2); base-prelude emitter recipes record the *current* per-prelude modes as migration truth (`:linear` for `py`, `:balanced` for `php`/`js`; the bundled `yang.clojure` continuation family is a LEFT FOLD, not balanced — recorded as its own mode so the freeze is exact) without changing shapes. | No golden churn for py/js/php (no shape change); new modules get fresh addresses | Closure, missing-manifest, `host-limits`, direct-provenance vs. transitive-footprint tests; 4-host test suite for `data/equiv` (`[0.0] == [-0.0]`, `[NaN] != [NaN]`, `(keyword nil \"a/b\") != (keyword \"a\" \"b\")`), `data/admit-key?`, `data/canonical-compare`/`canonical-entries`, and `yin.vm.float` (`2.1 // 0.7 == 3.0`, `-0.0 // 2.0 == -0.0`, `0.5 ** -2000 -> :underflow`, `format` `1.0 -> \"1.0\"`); existing py/php oracle suites unchanged-green. |\n648:| **P2′ — Unified `clojure.core` + `yang.clojure` migration** | Publish collision-free `clojure.core.impl` (pure, `impl-*` prefix, `admit-key?`-guarded) + cell-free `clojure.core` facade; migrate `yang.clojure` directly onto unified `clj` + `clojure.core`. | Refresh `yang.clojure` goldens cleanly | Native collection invocation through the new standard library (the locally-bound-map `:k` → 9 fixture) and bundled primitive shadowing of bare `get`/`assoc` (which otherwise resolve through the source store before VM primitives); unified `yang.clojure` suite green. The real `clj → clj.py → clj` cross-syntax unwind (cleanup + context restoration) gates ONLY at P3′, after `clj.py` exists. |\n651:| **Track B — Legacy prelude re-architecture (deferred, on demand)** | Migrate the native `py`/`js`/`php` preludes onto `yrt.effect`/`yrt.int`/boxed float (the r6 P1/P4 legs: 4→5-slot contexts, generators via `:gen/yield`, `yrt.safepoint`, `php.sp` integration per its own hooks); undertaken only when legacy demand justifies it. | Refresh py/js/php goldens per migration slice | The r6 P1/P4 gates apply verbatim at that time, attached here by value: generator + safepoint parity suites across VMs/hosts preserving PHP lifecycle/cleanup and Python `:base` rebasing; migration of `py`/`js`/`php` onto `yrt.effect`, `yrt.int`, and boxed `yin.vm.float` (4→5-slot contexts; `dsg__add`/`dsg__lte` for bundled `clj`); existing Python & PHP generator tests green; independent concurrent `py`/`js`/`php`/`clj` tasks sharing `yrt.*`; bundled == linked + 4-host + CPython/Node/PHP oracle parity; `clj ./bin/analyze-deps.clj` clean. |\n657:1. **D10 — Default-profile policy & legacy-track deferral (`Settled — r7 Owner Directive`):** For the parameterized frontends, the **Yin/Clojure profile is the DEFAULT** (`:yang.python/clojure-core-v1` first; ts/php to follow); the native preludes (`py`/`js`/`php` semantics) become the **Legacy compatibility track** — kept frozen as landed (they already exist at their current content addresses with passing oracle suites), with their `yrt.*`/boxed-float re-architecture deferred to Track B until legacy demand justifies it. The clojure prelude family is built first. Consequence named in §6.1: capability refusals (classes, generators, typed `except`, `with`, kwargs) are the default experience for source written against native semantics; pinning the legacy revision is the escape hatch.\n664:3. **D3 — Python float tagging (r7: moot until Track B — py keeps its tagged `{:py/float}` representation as-frozen; boxed `yin.vm.float` ships for the Clojure path in P0′):**\n665:   - *Option A (Recommended — Architect concurred):* Retain `{:py/float x}` behind a 2-line `py` boundary adapter around boxed `yin.vm.float` through P1 so Python's `1 == 1.0` oracle semantics stay cleanly isolated.\n673:   - Settled in favor of publishing collision-free `clojure.core.impl` + cell-free `clojure.core` AND migrating `yang.clojure` directly onto unified `clj` + `clojure.core` in P3 (retiring `yang.clojure`'s legacy `library-for` duplication and unit-local `dsg__call_token` path).\n674:7. **D7 — Float exponentiation rounding (r7: `fpow-half` ships in P0′ for the Clojure path; `fpow-base` defers to Track B with the php re-architecture):**\n678:   - Settled on: (1) `:pure` host value core (`yin.vm.data`, `yin.vm.integer`, boxed `yin.vm.float`, `kind/namespace`) for total, representation-sensitive ops; (2) unified guest algebraic effects (`yrt.effect` over `%capture`) for control flow, generators, and cold error/limit policy traps; (3) minimal VM/stream effects (`cell/*`, `stream/*`, `:module/require`) per ADR 0004.\n\n :yang.semantics/literals\n {:nil     {:kind :raw, :value nil}\n  :bool    {:kind :raw}\n  :str     {:kind :raw}\n  :float   {:kind :float64-raw}      ;; vs {:kind :tagged-map, :tag :py/float}\n  :int     {:kind :raw-or-call, :safe-max-bits 53, :overflow-op 'clj.py/int-lit}\n  :unbound {:kind :raw, :value :clj/unbound}}\n\n :yang.semantics/hooks\n {;; Arithmetic & comparisons — ALL namespace-qualified (hygienic, immune to guest shadowing)\n  :op/add           'clj.py/add\n  :op/sub           'clj.py/sub\n  :op/mul           'clj.py/mul\n  :op/truediv       'clj.py/truediv\n  :op/floordiv      'clj.py/floordiv\n  :op/mod           'clj.py/mod\n  :op/pow           'clj.py/pow\n  :op/neg           'clj.py/neg\n  :op/pos           'clj.py/pos\n  :op/eq            'clj.py/eq\n  :op/ne            'clj.py/ne\n  :op/lt            'clj.py/lt\n  :op/le            'clj.py/le\n  :op/gt            'clj.py/gt\n  :op/ge            'clj.py/ge\n  :op/lnot          'clj.py/lnot\n  :op/truthy        'clj.py/truthy\n  ;; Collections, indexing, and comprehension accumulators\n  :coll/vconj       'clj.py/vconj\n  :coll/list        'clj.py/list\n  :coll/tuple       'clj.py/tuple\n  :coll/set         'clj.py/set-from\n  :coll/dict        'clj.py/map-from\n  :coll/getitem     'clj.py/get-item\n  :comp/list-new    'clj.py/comp-list-new    ;; [init-vec] -> accumulator; py-v1: 'py/list\n  :comp/list-append 'clj.py/comp-list-append ;; [acc val] -> step result; py-v1: 'py/list-append\n  :comp/set-new     'clj.py/comp-set-new     ;; [] -> accumulator; py-v1: 'py/set-new\n  :comp/set-add     'clj.py/comp-set-add     ;; [acc val] -> step result; py-v1: 'py/set-add\n  :comp/dict-new    'clj.py/comp-dict-new    ;; [] -> accumulator; py-v1: 'py/dict-new\n  :comp/dict-set    'clj.py/comp-dict-set    ;; [acc k v] -> step result; py-v1: 'py/dict-set\n  :comp/finish      'clj.py/comp-finish      ;; optional [acc] -> final collection; nil in py-v1\n  ;; Scopes & bindings\n  :env/local-get    'clj.py/local-get\n  :env/global-get   'clj.py/global-get\n  :env/global-set   'clj.py/global-set\n  ;; Functions & calls\n  :fn/arg           'clj.py/arg\n  :fn/make          'clj.py/make-fn\n  :fn/call          'clj.py/call\n  ;; Control flow & unit entry (unit/run-main always takes `[body-fn ambient-resolver]`)\n  :ctrl/for-each    'clj.py/for-each\n  :ctrl/try         'clj.py/try\n  :ctrl/try-finally 'clj.py/try-finally\n  :ctrl/raise       'clj.py/raise\n  :ctrl/call-ec     'clj.py/call-ec\n  :unit/run-main    'clj.py/run-main}\n\n ;; Each entry defaults to :kind :cell-accessor (emitted per unit into `ambient-resolver` as\n ;; `(m/e)`, returning the module's stable task-local authenticated callable cell); optional\n ;; :kind :value references a non-lambda immutable export directly.\n :yang.semantics/ambient-projections\n {\"identity\"  {:module 'clojure.core, :export 'identity,  :kind :cell-accessor}\n  \"inc\"       {:module 'clojure.core, :export 'inc,       :kind :cell-accessor}\n  \"dec\"       {:module 'clojure.core, :export 'dec,       :kind :cell-accessor}\n  \"str\"       {:module 'clojure.core, :export 'str,       :kind :cell-accessor}\n  \"count\"     {:module 'clojure.core, :export 'count,     :kind :cell-accessor}\n  \"first\"     {:module 'clojure.core, :export 'first,     :kind :cell-accessor}\n  \"rest\"      {:module 'clojure.core, :export 'rest,      :kind :cell-accessor}\n  \"second\"    {:module 'clojure.core, :export 'second,    :kind :cell-accessor}\n  \"cons\"      {:module 'clojure.core, :export 'cons,      :kind :cell-accessor}\n  \"conj\"      {:module 'clojure.core, :export 'conj,      :kind :cell-accessor}\n  \"assoc\"     {:module 'clojure.core, :export 'assoc,     :kind :cell-accessor}\n  \"assoc_in\"  {:module 'clojure.core, :export 'assoc-in,  :kind :cell-accessor}\n  \"get\"       {:module 'clojure.core, :export 'get,       :kind :cell-accessor}\n  \"get_in\"    {:module 'clojure.core, :export 'get-in,    :kind :cell-accessor}\n  \"update\"    {:module 'clojure.core, :export 'update,    :kind :cell-accessor}\n  \"update_in\" {:module 'clojure.core, :export 'update-in, :kind :cell-accessor}\n  \"map\"       {:module 'clojure.core, :export 'map,       :kind :cell-accessor}\n  \"filter\"    {:module 'clojure.core, :export 'filter,    :kind :cell-accessor}\n  \"reduce\"    {:module 'clojure.core, :export 'reduce,    :kind :cell-accessor}\n  \"into\"      {:module 'clojure.core, :export 'into,      :kind :cell-accessor}\n  \"keys\"      {:module 'clojure.core, :export 'keys,      :kind :cell-accessor}\n  \"vals\"      {:module 'clojure.core, :export 'vals,      :kind :cell-accessor}\n  \"merge\"     {:module 'clojure.core, :export 'merge,     :kind :cell-accessor}\n  \"is_empty\"  {:module 'clojure.core, :export 'empty?,    :kind :cell-accessor}\n  \"is_nil\"    {:module 'clojure.core, :export 'nil?,      :kind :cell-accessor}\n  \"is_map\"    {:module 'clojure.core, :export 'map?,      :kind :cell-accessor}\n  \"is_vector\" {:module 'clojure.core, :export 'vector?,   :kind :cell-accessor}\n  \"is_set\"    {:module 'clojure.core, :export 'set?,      :kind :cell-accessor}\n  \"ex_info\"   {:module 'clj.py,       :export 'ex-info,   :kind :cell-accessor}}}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
