{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_11","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '20,100p' src/cljc/yang/core/uast.cljc; sed -n '425,474p' src/cljc/yin/vm/integer.cljc; sed -n '300,313p' docs/design/yang.preludes.md; sed -n '69,96p' collab/yang-base/1795211000000-dry-p0prime-full2.patch.txt\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_11","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '20,100p' src/cljc/yang/core/uast.cljc; sed -n '425,474p' src/cljc/yin/vm/integer.cljc; sed -n '300,313p' docs/design/yang.preludes.md; sed -n '69,96p' collab/yang-base/1795211000000-dry-p0prime-full2.patch.txt\"","aggregated_output":"  (:require\n    [yang.tails :as tails]\n    [yin.vm :as vm]))\n\n\n(defn lit\n  [x]\n  {:type :literal, :value x})\n\n\n(defn v\n  [sym]\n  {:type :variable, :name sym})\n\n\n(defn lam\n  [params body]\n  {:type :lambda, :params (vec params), :body body})\n\n\n(defn app\n  [op & args]\n  {:type :application, :operator op, :operands (vec args)})\n\n\n(defn if-node\n  [t c a]\n  {:type :if, :test t, :consequent c, :alternate a})\n\n\n(def capture {:type :vm/current-continuation})\n\n\n(defn def!\n  \"`(yin/def key value)`: key is a literal symbol.\"\n  [key value]\n  (app (v 'yin/def) (lit key) value))\n\n\n(def discard\n  \"The parameter a sequencing lambda binds and ignores. `%` cannot begin a\n   Python identifier, so it never shadows a guest name.\"\n  '%_)\n\n\n(defn then\n  \"Evaluate `a` for effect, then `b`.\"\n  [a b]\n  (app (lam [discard] b) a))\n\n\n(defn seq-nodes\n  \"Evaluate every node in order; the value is the last one's.\"\n  [nodes]\n  (reduce (fn [acc node] (then acc node)) (first nodes) (rest nodes)))\n\n\n(defn let1\n  [sym value body]\n  (app (lam [sym] body) value))\n\n\n(defn sexp->uast\n  [form]\n  (cond\n    (symbol? form) (v form)\n    (seq? form)\n    (let [[head & args] form]\n      (case head\n        fn (lam (first args) (sexp->uast (second args)))\n        if (if-node (sexp->uast (first args))\n                    (sexp->uast (second args))\n                    (sexp->uast (nth args 2)))\n        do (seq-nodes (map sexp->uast args))\n        let (let [[bindings body] args]\n              (reduce (fn [inner [sym value]]\n                        (let1 sym (sexp->uast value) inner))\n                      (sexp->uast body)\n                      (reverse (partition 2 bindings))))\n        quote (lit (first args))\n        %capture capture\n    (ratio->float (magnitude x) (magnitude y)\n                  (not= (neg? (sign x)) (neg? (sign y))))))\n\n\n(defn- float!\n  \"Argument `arg` of `op` as a host double, or a `:wrong-type` refusal.\"\n  [op arg v]\n  (if (host/host-float? v) v (wrong-type! op arg :float)))\n\n\n(defn- int-compare-float\n  [_limits a f]\n  (let [x (big! 'compare-float 0 a)\n        v (float! 'compare-float 1 f)]\n    (cond\n      (host/nan-float? v) (wrong-type! 'compare-float 1 :non-nan-float)\n      (host/infinite-float? v) (if (pos? v) -1 1)\n      :else\n      ;; t = trunc(v): x < t means x < v, x > t means x >= t + 1 > v\n      ;; (or x > t >= v when v is negative); x = t leaves the fraction\n      (let [c (host/compare-big x (float-kernel/trunc-big v))]\n        (cond (not (zero? c)) c\n              (or (>= (float-kernel/signed (neg? v) v) two-53-float)\n                  (= v (host/native->double (host/trunc-native v))))\n              0\n              (pos? v) -1\n              :else 1)))))\n\n\n(defn- int-from-float\n  [limits f]\n  (let [v (float! 'from-float 0 f)]\n    (if (or (host/nan-float? v) (host/infinite-float? v))\n      (wrong-type! 'from-float 0 :finite-float)\n      (out limits (float-kernel/trunc-big v)))))\n\n\n;; =============================================================================\n;; Text\n;; =============================================================================\n\n(def ^:private digit-values\n  \"Each digit character, either letter case, to its value.\"\n  (into {}\n        (mapcat (fn [i]\n                  (let [c (subs \"0123456789abcdefghijklmnopqrstuvwxyz\" i (inc i))]\n                    [[c i] [(str/upper-case c) i]])))\n        (range 36)))\n\n\n\n### 5.2 Composition rules and verified-closure admission\n\n`yang.core.prelude` and `yang.core.prelude-admission` enforce six fail-closed checks. **Home rule (DRY-alignment, r7):** the composition checks (`validate-profile`, `admit-profile`, and their six sub-checks) are implemented in **`yang.core.prelude-admission`** (3 → 5 publics, exactly at the bounded-complexity target), keeping `yang.core.prelude` pure UAST/s-expression emission — the emission/admission boundary is the landed batch-1 seam (`1604aabe`), and the C2 lesson (module duplicating prelude's `host-declaration` was the duplication removed) requires one admission authority, not two namespaces sharing the checks:\n\n1. **Verified artifact closure input (`validate-profile`):** Takes `(profile artifact-store registry)`, where `artifact-store` supplies an immutable content-addressed map of published manifests (`manifest-addr -> verified-manifest`) AND their referenced canonical module trees (`tree-addr -> verified-uast`). Verifies that direct root pins match `:yang.prelude/components`, walks the full transitive `:requires` DAG from `:yang.prelude/root-address`, confirms finiteness and acyclicity, and refuses duplicate bindings for the same linker module symbol.\n2. **Export collision rule (qualified vs. projected):** Distinct Layer-2a/2b/2c modules may share bare local export names across qualified module borders; collisions are refused on duplicate linker module symbols, duplicate stripped local `module-definitions` keys, or duplicate source-facing `:ambient-projections` aliases (`§6.3`).\n3. **Provenance-door security exclusion (direct declarations, not transitive footprint):** Checks each non-trusted module's (`yrt.*`, `clj.py`, `clojure.core.impl`, `clojure.core`) **direct** `:yin.module/primitives` (refusing `cell/dsg__new-provenance` and `cell/dsg__provenance`) and **direct** `:yin.module/exports` (refusing any `dsg__*` export on **every** module including trusted Layer-2b runtimes), while governing transitive `:yin.module/footprint` through `:yang.prelude/max-effects`.\n4. **Effect-ceiling verification (`:yang.prelude/max-effects`):** Optional ceiling checked via `(clojure.set/subset? derived-transitive-effects max-effects)` over the verified `:yin.module/footprint :effects` union.\n5. **Host-module and limit admission (`admit-profile`):** Takes `(profile artifact-store registry host-limits)`, verifies every required host export (`prelude-admission/admit`), and enforces declared numeric floors (`:min-bits`, `:min-digits`, `:min-max-items`) against `host-limits` (failing closed if absent or below floor).\n6. **Dual-emitter standardization & Parity Law:** Standardized linked emission applies to the **P0′ Clojure-family modules** (`:trailing-requires []`, `:finalize-c1? true`) — it does NOT retroactively standardize the frozen native preludes (r8: landed `py` ends its module tree with `require yang.call` and has no C1 finalizer there; php likewise; the bundled clojure continuation family is a left fold — the `:mode` field alone cannot freeze these, so each frozen runtime records its bundled shape, linked trailing forms, dependency pins, and C1 side-table identity-or-absence **independently**). Any program compiled under a composed prelude MUST produce identical outcomes in bundled and linked modes across the semantic, stack, and register VMs (and the AST walker once L-b lands).\n\n---\n\n+\n+\n+(defn- module-definitions\n+  \"Collect definitions in evaluated expressions, including immediately invoked\n+   lambda bodies, without descending into literals or function values.\"\n+  [ast]\n+  (loop [todo [ast] defs []]\n+    (if-let [node (peek todo)]\n+      (let [todo (pop todo)]\n+        (case (:type node)\n+          :application\n+          (let [op (:operator node)\n+                definition? (and (= :variable (:type op)) (= 'yin/def (:name op)))\n+                todo (into todo (:operands node))\n+                todo (conj todo (if (= :lambda (:type op)) (:body op) op))]\n+            (recur todo (if definition? (conj defs (get-in node [:operands 0 :value])) defs)))\n+          :if (recur (into todo [(:test node) (:consequent node) (:alternate node)]) defs)\n+          (recur todo defs)))\n+      defs)))\n+\n+\n+(defn- profile-closure [profile store registry]\n+  (let [required #{:yang.prelude/schema :yang.prelude/id :yang.prelude/revision\n+                   :yang.prelude/module :yang.prelude/root-address\n+                   :yang.prelude/components :yang.prelude/host-modules\n+                   :yang.prelude/max-effects}\n+        components (:yang.prelude/components profile)]\n+    (when-not (and (map? profile) (portable-data? profile) (= required (set (keys profile)))\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
